s possible.\n\nThe valid pairs \\((b, c)\\) are \\((3, 4)\\), \\((3, 5)\\), \\((3, 6)\\), \\((4, 4)\\), \\((4, 5)\\), \\((4, 6)\\), \\((5, 5)\\), \\((5, 6)\\), \\((6, 6)\\).\n\nWe now count the total number of valid four-digit numbers \\( N \\):\n\n\\[\n\\text{Total valid } N = 2 \\times (3 + 4 + 5)\n\\]\n\nHere, we have 2 choices for \\( a \\), and \\( b \\) and \\( c \\) can each take any of the valid 6 values.\n\nSo we calculate:\n\n\\[\n\\text{Total valid } N = 2 \\times 12 = 24\n\\]\n\nThen, we count the number of ways to fill in each position:\n\n- \\( a \\) has 2 choices (4 or 5).\n- \\( d \\) has 2 choices (0 or 5).\n\nThus, the total number of valid four-digit numbers is:\n\n\\[\n2 \\times 2 = 4\n\\]\n\nHence, the number of four-digit numbers \\( N \\) that satisfy the given conditions is:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{4}\n\\]",
